    "department: 119 of 119 rows have known values (100.0% coverage).",
    "At k = 20, mean shared-label agreement is 100.0% when weighting positive anchor\u2013label pairs, and 100.0% when weighting labels equally. Mean individual label lift is 3 and equal-label lift is 3.032. Mean lift is not aggregate purity divided by aggregate chance.",
    "outdoors: 45 known positives; 45 evaluable positive anchors have 100.0% mean agreement, versus 37.8% reference prevalence (lift 2.644). An average of 20 of 20 neighbors have known annotations. Large lift for a rare label can coexist with low agreement.",
    "books: 39 known positives; 39 evaluable positive anchors have 100.0% mean agreement, versus 32.8% reference prevalence (lift 3.051). An average of 20 of 20 neighbors have known annotations. Large lift for a rare label can coexist with low agreement.",
    "kitchen: 35 known positives; 35 evaluable positive anchors have 100.0% mean agreement, versus 29.4% reference prevalence (lift 3.4). An average of 20 of 20 neighbors have known annotations. Large lift for a rare label can coexist with low agreement.",
    "Known-neighbor coverage at this k is 100.0%. Unknown neighbors are excluded from agreement denominators; missing annotations can bias the result.",
    "The saved null comparison gives an empirical one-sided p-value of 0.25 for macro_lift. This tests the specified shuffle, not semantic understanding; use the combined multiple-testing table and practical effect sizes when judging the finding.",
    "The probe panel measures recoverability on a held-out split. Compare each model with its baseline; recoverability and nearest-neighbor usefulness answer different questions.",
    "baseline: balanced_accuracy 0.3333, macro_f1 0.1709; 29 held-out test rows (or the macro summary of supported binary tags).",
    "linear: balanced_accuracy 1, macro_f1 1; 29 held-out test rows (or the macro summary of supported binary tags).",
